# R example scripts for the distribution-fitting appendix are teaching
# material, not part of the KSL library. Exclude them from GitHub's
# language statistics (Linguist) so they don't show up in the language bar.
*.R linguist-documentation

# Check Kotlin sources out as LF on every platform. The build-time indexer behind
# the KSL code MCP server parses .kt through the Kotlin compiler's PSI, which
# requires \n-only text. A CRLF working tree (Git for Windows defaults
# core.autocrlf=true) silently emptied the package of 61% of the generated index.
*.kt text eol=lf
